00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:01.350 align:start position:0%
 
all right it's fair to say that  battlefield 2042's beta could have been  better after the press preview event and  the limited early access beta  battlefield 2042 opened the floodgates  for a weekend allowing everyone to gain  access to the beta and reactions were  understandably mixed the rose tinted  lenses are off now and some of my  initial hype has died down despite my  earlier video where i had almost nothing  but praise and excitement for the beta  so let's break down some key parts of  the beta now that it's fully wrapped up  and see what was good and what looks  like it needs some serious work ahead of  the full game's release obligatory shout  out for your likes and subs because come  on now it's battlefield we're gonna have  a lot more to share with you leading up  to launch and you won't want to miss it  so good news you're bad news let's start  with the good news first yeah so right  off the bat there was a lot of curiosity  on how battlefield 2042 would handle  destruction and to that a good old  tornado would like to introduce itself  the tornado is an absolute highlight in  my honest opinion and is one that i  think a lot of other folks agree with it  is an awesome in-game event that can  happen totally at random and at  different parts of the map it's pretty  novel right now and there could come a  time where that wears off but as of  right now the tornado is a highlight to  me plain and simple alongside the  tornado destruction makes its return  although maybe not quite to the extent  of bad company 2's awesome destruction  where you could just level buildings  into the ground but still i've seen a  few distinct videos from reddit or  youtube showing off really awesome  destruction  that makes me really hopeful for  destruction at launch on all the other  maps after all battlefield is nothing  without destruction so it is absolutely  no surprise to me that the chaos of  destruction and levolution passes this  initial test  all right not quite bad but not exactly  great either the graphics seem to have a  mix of reactions barring xbox one and  ps4 players most of the players in the  beta probably got to enjoy the pretty  solid overall visuals of the game on  xbox series x ps5 and pc although that  is totally subjective which is okay  there may very well be a bunch of you in  the comments that thought the game  looked awful which i understand i played  the beta on pc and despite the visual  bugs and glitches i thought the game  looked okay for what it was to be honest  after all i was more focused on  maximizing my time with the build i also  think that the game being just maybe one  or two steps above the graphics of  battlefield 4 is a necessary evil since  we're ramping up the lobby size to 128  players on pc and current gen consoles  trade-offs with in-game graphics for  performance are gonna be necessary which  explains why i'm probably gonna see  folks making war zone comparisons in  terms of the visual fidelity  this one might be controversial but i  was actually really enjoying my time  with the specialists mckay is my guy i  love the intrinsic perks and the added  dynamism to the meta with having these  specialists reading more online and  talking to friends and colleagues alike  that played the beta i can see the  downside of the specialists too they  come at the expense of the original  battlefield classes classes were the  backbone of the battlefield player  giving you a customizable loadout within  a boundary based on what kind of a  playstyle you wanted the assault  engineer support and recon classes were  all meant to be played a certain way and  their kits supported that playstyle with  specialists that's kind of out the  window sure your specialist ability  tries to keep you in that framework for  example you're not gonna be scouting  with folk you know her healing dart  still puts her squarely in that medic  role but you can still take out  helicopters with anti-air rockets like  something just doesn't fit i easily  ignored most of this when i was playing  the beta because it is a video game if  i'm gonna suspend my disbelief and  grapple onto a rocket launcher up to the  ozone i can believe that falk is capable  of blowing up a couple of helicopters i  pick my battles so yeah i personally  thought specialists were fun but plenty  of people out there preferred the  operators of old and i can completely  see where they're coming from if  anything i'm gonna make a bold claim and  say that it's not the specialists that  are a big problem it's the non-class  specific weapons and gadgetry there are  too many people running around with  launchers and no one is playing support  battlefield is all about squads and  synergy among the chaos and right now  all we have are a bunch of chaos and a  bunch of lone wolves  all right customization has been another  hot topic among the community and from  what i understand also a mixed result  personally i welcome change i don't  always like it but i find that when  mechanics and gameplay changes knew that  the battlefield franchise are applied  the potential grows a perfect example is  the in-game attachment system also  referred to as the plus system i like it  i really do i know a lot of folks will  disagree which is okay honestly but it's  just how i feel it feels nice being able  to swap from iron sights to a red dot  and to mess with different parts of the  gun on the fly the system could totally  be just a gimmick which many content  creators seem to feel is the case but i  don't know if you've seen my other  videos you know that i'm obsessed with  destiny and that game is all about  tweaking your loadout and build crafting  so this kind of light express style  customization is totally in my  wheelhouse but i understand if it feels  unnecessary to others  alright your mileage may vary here  particularly if you're on controller  versus mouse and keyboard but the  vehicles in the beta did not feel good  to me at all  like at all i couldn't get in the swing  of things and call me crazy but if a  vehicle is handling worse than a warthog  from halo we have a problem the call-in  vehicle system was interesting but it  also felt a little off after some time  similar to the in-game attachment plus  system calling in vehicles didn't really  stick with players like dice may have  hoped although once again this beta is  from an older build and we only had like  half a week to really see it in action  i'm confident that the more players use  these systems in practice over time the  more normalized and viable these  additions become but the core gameplay  loop of those vehicles  yeah not so good  i was a fan of the huge verticality that  one building offered and the orbital map  as well as the rocket launch station  directly across from it the rest of the  map though was whatever it was also huge  despite it being considered one of the  more moderate sized maps orbital was  also just super open which felt boring  after a while especially on the infantry  side of things vehicles will thrive and  an important factor to help navigate  these maps is bringing things like that  colon system into a necessity but as  mentioned earlier the handling on those  vehicles just sucked like i cannot get  over that they really do feel like they  go hand in hand it doesn't help that  conquest is the bread and butter of  battlefield and that game mode doesn't  just sit as well with these large maps  as it may have in battlefield 3 or 4.  the levolution is excellent as  levolutions tend to be but there's very  little else about orbital that felt like  something worth championing which is  unfortunate battlefield maps can be hit  or miss depending on which game you're  playing but they all tend to have  distinct characteristics or aesthetics  short of the rocket launch everything  else about orbital felt incredibly dull  especially after my initial excitement  wore off from the first several matches  i think poor optimization has to be the  standout for me out of all the things  that could be the worst takeaway from  the beta my colleagues and friends  started telling me that they could  barely get the game to run not long  after my initial preview for the beta  went live the optimism that i originally  had started to dwindle as i continued to  play i played on pc throughout the  entire beta and my rig isn't top of the  line but it's definitely not bad either  even with a 1080 ti and an i9 processor  i had to lower the graphic settings down  a few notches because i was running into  performance issues now imagine the  frustration of folks online with 30 80s  saying that they were running into less  than ideal frame rates and all of this  doesn't even scratch the surface of  significant issues people face trying to  play on console last gen support needs  to be dropped from large online  multiplayer games in my mind going  forward this might be a controversial  statement with the lack of readily  available next-gen consoles due to  garbage scalpers but the truth is that  old gen hardware is significantly  hindering games like battlefield 2042  that are trying to push barriers with  their ambition you can't have massive  maps in huge 128 player lobbies on old  architecture xbox one and ps4 just  cannot keep up and those builds suffered  the most visual glitches long load times  and having trouble even just getting the  game to work on those platforms makes  the whole experience awful there were  persisting problems that went beyond  last gen consoles unfortunately poor  optimization leads to less than ideal  experiences for ps5 and series x owners  as well although not nearly as bad as  those on the xbox one and ps4 i'm still  telling myself that if dice chooses to  move forward with the recently delayed  november release the game will be in a  significantly better state than the beta  that we received however the reports of  poor performance across the board in  some capacity or another are concerning  listen man all of this aside i'm holding  the faith whatever dice decides to do i  am going to support and i expect growing  pains nothing is ever perfect and in  2021 games are almost expected to have  post launch support for a very long time  i hope that battlefield only has to deal  with launch day server issues  temporarily because it's bound to not be  pretty if the issues listed earlier  continue let's not understate all the  good that we got to glimpse from the  beta despite the negatives and please  keep in mind that this build was old by  several months and whatever dice is  currently iterating right now is not the  same as what we played also note that we  only saw one game mode and map and that  the core gameplay loop was still as  solid as ever firefights are fun and  weapon engagements are a thrill despite  some balance issues you have levolutions  and extreme weather events like the  tornadoes triumphantly demanding  attention each match which is a delight  to me not to mention we still have  battlefield portal in the brand new  hazard zone to look forward to i am  confident that if there are any issues  dice will be sure to do their damnedest  to fix them if they could do it with  battlefield 4 they can do it here sound  off in the comments what you thought and  be sure to tell me what you're hopeful  for with battlefield 2042 if you clicked  on this video odds are you love  battlefield and you want the best for  this game just like i do so i welcome  all of your thoughts tell me what you  hope to see in the comments below and  we'll share as we learn more about  hazard zone or any other big news on  battlefield until next time

